@DarkDragon76
- Looks like you might have an older version of the software. If you would be so kind, re-download the software using the same link as in the main post (it was updated fairly recently). Then give it another try - if it still doesn't work, the log file should at least give more detailed information
Thanks!

To be fair, I did not make this wonderful piece of software,
@Backlash404
did, which he initially made for his own uses but decided to allow me to release it publically since it could be very helpful. Originally you had to put together your characters in GIMP or Photoshop or whatever other image manipulation program you like. The fact that the software is pretty easy to use and works specifically for these resources and is free is a huge boon, one that I give full credit to Backlash404.
As
@jayray
pointed out, you can definitely expand the quantity of templates with just a little bit of minor editing. Also, if you only have one or two packs, then you would have a small number of templates. These packs are generally meant to build on top of previous packs, further growing an ever-increasing library of resources, templates included. Most packs have 3 templates per gender, and the freebies pack gives some additional free templates.
@CanSim
- That is an issue with the software unfortunatley. It is coded to recognize just the human shadows I think, and unfortunately I have not heard word from the creator in awhile so I am unsure as to if it can be patched to allow for different shadows. For now, you can create the Dwarven character without the shadow and then just manually drop the shadow in with GIMP or Photoshop. My apologies for the inconvenience!

@jcoultas
- Regarding the license and two people using assets - each person would need to purchase the resources in order for both people to have a license for the resources. I am pretty sure that is how all of the RPG Maker resource packs work.
@aston00
- It is hard for me to say exactly as I didn't make the software, but I think there is a memory leak (or at least the capacity to overload the memory) for the software that causes that. I run into that issue if I try to make 3 or 4 or more characters consecutively, but I can avoid it by making 1 or 2 characters and then restarting the software before it has a chance. Depending on your computer hardware, you might be reaching that limit faster than others. Unfortunately there isn't really anything I can do about it though, the creator seems to have stepped away and I do not think there will be more updates to address these sorts of bugs.

