Here is a character created with the software opened in photoshop so you can see what I mean with the transparency issue. It seems to be from the hair.

@Backlash404
I hope you get the chance to read this. Thank you. Deep respect and infinite gratitude. I know developing this and adding to it and changing it and keeping it all working and supporting it all for free must have been a nightmare with seemingly no reward at times. We all have used these assets without a character creation generator in the past and dreamed of having something simpler. You literally gave it to us. The game development world needs more people like you...who make our dreams a reality.
@Jesse - PVGames
Thank you for all of the amazing assets you have created and shared and for seeking to make your users even happier by providing tips and tricks on how to use them and get more mileage out of them. I'm sure it was a dream come true and a godsend to be able to answer all of the requests for a character generator with this. I wish you the best as you continue your endeavors.

@MLyons
For the map (character) view you want any of the files that show 3 images of a character across and 4 rows deep. By default, MV uses character sheets that have this format pasted 4 times across with another row of 4 under that so you only need 1 file to store map (character) view sprites for 8 characters. Hence, you need to increase the image size of whichever of the files you decided on that I mentioned before to be 4x the original pixel width and 2x the original pixel height. So just take your desired file into PhotoShop if you have it, GIMP if you don't (GIMP is free to download and similar to PhotoShop), open your desired file, and change the canvas size 4x as wide and 2x as tall and save it out and you should be able to use that in MV. Hope it helps!
EDIT: Please note you are just changing the dimensions of the image itself, not scaling anything. Changing the dimensions will create a large blank space, but MV by default only looks at the horizontal of these images 1/4 at a time and only the top or bottom 1/2 when framing the cursor you use to select which of the 8 characters it thinks you have on the sheet, so...you should be good.

@MLyons
- Correct - to be fair, the formats of these graphics predate the plugins for MV, if you're wondering why it ended up that way
The new software that is being developed will not have these issues due to its flexible nature. You will be able to have it export sheets however you want it to, including in the format you are looking for.

